%description:

Tcp.rfc5961AckCheck:off -- a very old ACK is an old duplicate: host1 sends no ACK in reply.

The claim (Tcp.ned): "the ACK check of RFC 5961 section 5.2, which RFC 9293 allows (MAY-12) and
Linux uses: a segment whose ACK lies below SND.UNA - MAX.SND.WND is dropped, and an ACK goes in
reply; false: such an ACK counts as an old duplicate ACK".

The classes: off (false, the default) and on (true, the value of LinuxTcp). The code:
TcpConnection::processAckInEstabEtc() drops a segment whose ACK is below SND.UNA - MAX.SND.WND
and sends an ACK, with true; with false, the ACK is an old duplicate, which changes nothing. This test separates "off" from "on".

Host under test: host1, which sends 300000 bytes; host2 offers 65535 bytes. The tap writes the
ACK number {isn} + 1 + 10000, far below SND.UNA - 65535, into the first ACK of host2 that
acknowledges more than 200000 bytes. host1 sends no other pure ACK after the handshake. Observation: level 1, host1 sends no pure ACK in 0.5 s after the old ACK.

%# parameter: Tcp.rfc5961AckCheck
%# class: off
%# value: false
%# key: *.host1.tcp.rfc5961AckCheck
%# expected-result: PASS

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("TcpRfc5961AckCheckOff")
        .intercept(tap("tap").from("host2").filterPacket("tcp.ackNo > {isn} + 1 + 200000").nth(1).set("tcp.ackNo", "{isn} + 1 + 10000")
                     .describe("the first ACK of host2 above 200000 bytes: an old ACK number"))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true && tcp.ackBit == false")
             .capture("isn", "tcp.sequenceNo")
             .describe("the SYN of host1")
             .within(0.5))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetReceivedFromLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.ackNo == {isn} + 1 + 10000")
             .describe("the old ACK at host1")
             .within(2.0))
        .never(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
              .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == false && tcp.finBit == false && tcp.rstBit == false && pk.dataLength <= tcp.headerLength")
              .describe("an ACK of host1 in reply")
              .within(0.5));
}

%activity:
EV << "TcpRfc5961AckCheckOff compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host1.tcp.rfc5961AckCheck = false    # the parameter under test
*.host1.app[0].sendBytes = 300000B
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST TcpRfc5961AckCheckOff: PASS
